invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: crt_combine returns without wiping t, which ends as the limbs of
  qinv after it held the second half of the signature modulo p. Inside a
  signature a later call's frame is written over that one, so
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test calls the recombination on its own
  (test/rsa_sign_equiv_pieces.c), copies the stack below it and finds two
  limbs of the value there.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_mul_add(s, mod_q->m, h, m2, k);
    ct_wipe(t, sizeof t);
--- new
    rsa_mont64_mul_add(s, mod_q->m, h, m2, k);
